COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[589,"§Al-Inshiqaq\ndeeds\nListen to the recitation of the Quran with reflection.\nWhen you reach the verse of prostration in this Surah, prostrate.\nStarting today, ensure to begin doing things using the right-hand side in all of your good affairs.\nguid\nSome of the horrors of the Day of Resurrection are described here.\nSubmit to Allah as other creatures do.\nThis is a threat to the deniers.\nrefl\nعَلَى ٱلۡأَرَآئِكِ يَنظُرُونَ ٣٥\nMeaning: They will be gazing at the gardens, rivers, fair women, and boys of everlasting youth. They will have nothing else to do except that and similar pleasures. Imam Al-Qushayri said: Here, Allah mentions their gaze but not what they will be gazing at because they gaze at different things: Some will be gazing at their palaces, others will gaze at their fair woman, and so on. The elite among them will always be gazing at Allah, the Almighty, while the wicked will always be barred from that. Al-Biqai: 21/327.\nAllah mentions their gaze but not what they will be gazing at. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ إِنَّكَ كَادِحٌ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ كَدۡحٗا فَمُلَٰقِيهِ ٦\nAllah encourages people to strive to the best in their deeds, for whoever surely believes that he will be brought to Judgement before the King, will do his utmost in every good deed to win the praise when meeting Him. Al-Biqai: 21/339.\nWhat should be the servant's duty when he realizes that he will meet Allah?\nوَيَنقَلِبُ إِلَىٰٓ أَهۡلِهِۦ مَسۡرُورٗا ٩\nThis is in contrast to what he used to be in worldly life. He was apprehensive of being brought to Judgement before Allah, distressed, afflicted with hardship, and he reckoned with himself harshly day and night while facing difficulties with his family, in his livelihood, and against the evil of his opponents. Al-Biqai: 21/341.\nThe believer will be rewarded with joy with his family in Paradise. Why?\nوَأَمَّا مَنۡ أُوتِيَ كِتَٰبَهُۥ وَرَآءَ ظَهۡرِهِۦ ١٠\nDistinguishing the disbelievers by giving them their Records from behind their backs because the givers may not stand to look at their darkened ugly faces, or due to their abhorrence for them, or because the disbelievers cast Allah's Book behind their backs in worldly life. Al-Alusi: 30/81.\nThe disbeliever will be given his book from behind his back. Why?\nإِنَّهُۥ كَانَ فِيٓ أَهۡلِهِۦ مَسۡرُورًا ١٣\nMeaning: He was happy and did not think about the consequences, nor feared what was coming to him, but his short happiness led him to a long grief. Ibn Kathir: 4/490.\nWhen does happiness become censured?\nإِنَّهُۥ ظَنَّ أَن لَّن يَحُورَ ١٤\nThis kind of thought is an indication of the fact that denying or doubting the resurrection leads to every evil conduct and wastes the chance to do every good deed. Moreover, the belief in the Hereafter leads to every good deed and prevents from doing every evil deed. The belief in the resurrection is the basis of all righteous deeds, as it is mentioned in the beginning of the Quran: (A guidance for the righteous). Al-Shanqiti: 8/471.\nDenying or doubting the resurrection leads to every evil conduct. How?\nبَلَىٰٓۚ إِنَّ رَبَّهُۥ كَانَ بِهِۦ بَصِيرٗا ١٥\nMeaning: Allah looks at His servant in a perfect way, and is aware of him completely, hence, neglecting him while being aware of his actions contradicts Allah's wisdom, justice and sovereignty; this cannot be conceived by reason. Al-Biqai: 21/345.\nWhat does this statement (Indeed, his Lord was ever seeing him) indicate?\nwords\nانشَقَّتSplit open with clouds\nوَأَذِنَت لِرَبِّهَاObeys its Lord\nمُدَّتStretched flat and spread out\nيَدعُو ثُبُورًاCry out for destruction\nلَن يَحُورَHe would never return to Allah\nوَسَقَWhat it covers\nاتَّسَقَIt becomes full\nطَبَقًا عَن طَبَقٍVarious stages, sperm-drop to clinging clot, life to death to resurrection"],[590,"§Al-Buruj, Al-Inshiqaq\ndeeds\nRemind a Muslim or many to endure patiently with adversities in the cause of Allah.\nLend a hand to an oppressed fellow Muslim.\nRemind one or more Muslims that Allah is All-Forgiving and Most Affectionate.\nguid\nLearning from the example of the believers of past nations and the sacrifices that they made to be steadfast in faith.\nAllah retaliates for His allies against His enemies.\nRepenting from inflicting harm on the believers is obligatory.\nrefl\nوَشَاهِدٖ وَمَشۡهُودٖ ٣\nAmong Allah's creation, there is the witness and the witnessed, by which the world order is set. Hence, if a created being can become a witness, keeper, and watchful over others, then surely the Creator, the Almighty, is a Witness, all Aware of them, and Watchful over them. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/278.\nAllah states that among His creation, there is the witness and the witnessed. Why?\nقُتِلَ أَصۡحَٰبُ ٱلۡأُخۡدُودِ ٤ ٱلنَّارِ ذَاتِ ٱلۡوَقُودِ ٥\nOur scholars said: In this verse, Allah informs the believers of this Ummah about the adversities faced by the believers before them, to console them. The Prophet (ﷺ) related to them the story of the Boy, [Sahih Muslim-3005], so they would endure adversities and hardships patiently, and follow the example of the Boy in his patience, strong resolve, and sacrifice of himself to make known his message and bring people into Allah's religion, with his young age and great patience. Al-Qurtubi: 22/192-193.\nWhy does Allah relate to us the story of the people of the Trench?\nٱلَّذِي لَهُۥ مُلۡكُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ وَٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ شَهِيدٌ ٩\n(To Whom belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth), as He created them and all who dwell in them are His servants, and He controls them as the owner controls what he owns. (And Allah is witness over all things) because He knows, hears and sees all. Should these rebellious ones who oppose Allah not fear that the Almighty, the Omnipotent, wreak vengeance, or do they not realize that they are all servants of Him, and no one has any power over anyone else except with the permission of the Sovereign? Or is it hidden from them that Allah encompasses all what they do and will requite them for their actions? Rather, the disbelievers live in delusion and the wrongdoers are ignorant and blind to the straight path. Al-Saadi: 918.\nAllah mentions that the dominion of the heavens and earth belongs to Him after relating the story of the people of the Trench. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ فَتَنُواْ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتِ ثُمَّ لَمۡ يَتُوبُواْ فَلَهُمۡ عَذَابُ جَهَنَّمَ وَلَهُمۡ عَذَابُ ٱلۡحَرِيقِ ١٠\nAl-Hasan Al-Basri said: \"Look at this generosity and kindness; these people killed Allah's allies and He still invites them to repent and seek forgiveness.\" Ibn Kathir: 4/497.\nWhich part of this verse indicates the great generosity of Allah?\nوَهُوَ ٱلۡغَفُورُ ٱلۡوَدُودُ ١٤\nIt is said that affection is pure love. There is a subtle meaning here, for alongside His name (the Most Affectionate) He mentions His name (the All-Forgiving), to indicate that if the sinners repent to Allah and turn to Him, He will forgive their sins and love them. Al-Saadi: 919.\nWhat is the secret of joining these two names of Allah, (All-Forgiving, the Most Affectionate)?\nهَلۡ أَتَىٰكَ حَدِيثُ ٱلۡجُنُودِ ١٧ فِرۡعَوۡنَ وَثَمُودَ ١٨\nThis is a consolation to the Prophet (ﷺ) that the disbelievers among his people would meet the fate of the soldiers. Meaning: You have received the soldiers' news and knew what they did and what was done to them, so remind your people of the days of Allah, and warn them, lest befall them what had befallen those before them. Al-Alusi: 30/39.\nThis verse contains a threat and a warning to the disbelievers of Quraish. Explain.\nبَلۡ هُوَ قُرۡءَانٞ مَّجِيدٞ ٢١ فِي لَوۡحٖ مَّحۡفُوظِۢ ٢٢\n([inscribed] in a Preserved Tablet), protected from alteration, addition or deletion, and is guarded against the devils. It is the Preserved Tablet in which Allah has written down all things. This is indicative of the majesty and greatness of the Quran, and its high esteem with Allah. Al-Saadi: 919.\nDiscuss the status of the Quran with Allah, the Almighty.\nwords\nغَيرُ مَمنُونٍUninterrupted, and never ends\nذَاتِ البُرُوجِStations through which the sun and moon pass\nوَاليَومِ المَوعُودِThe Day of Resurrection\nوَشَاهِدٍ وَمَشهُودٍSwearing by the witness and the witnessed\nقُتِلَCursed, destroyed\nأَصحَابُ الأُخدُودِThe makers of the trench\nعَذَابُ الـحَرِيقِPunishment of the burning fire\nالوَدُودُThe Most Affectionate toward His allies, and loved by them"],[591,"§At-Tariq, Al-A'la\ndeeds\nRecall a sin you had committed that no one knew about, then ask for Allah's forgiveness.\nReview or memorize a Surah.\nShare a message as a reminder to fear Allah.\nguid\nRemember your creation from a sperm-drop, lest you become arrogant.\nThose who turn away from the guidance of Allah should beware of His respite.\nMan should be mindful of the deeds of his heart and hidden sins, for Allah is aware of all things.\nrefl\nيَوۡمَ تُبۡلَى ٱلسَّرَآئِرُ ٩\nMeaning: All man's hidden intents will appear, whether good or evil and his faith or disbelief, as Ibn Omar (k) said: On the Day of Resurrection, Allah will reveal every secret and it will appear on the faces as either good or evil. Al-Qurtubi: 22/221-214.\nHow will man's secrets be disclosed on the Day of Resurrection?\nيَوۡمَ تُبۡلَى ٱلسَّرَآئِرُ ٩\nThere is a subtle meaning in referring to the deeds as (secrets). Deeds are the result of hidden intents, so whoever has righteous hidden intents, his deeds will be righteous, and his face will shine with modesty. In contrast, whoever has corrupt hidden intents, his deeds will be corrupt regardless of how they appear, and his hidden intent will cast darkness upon his face. In worldly life, only his outward deeds are visible, not his intents, but on the Day of Resurrection, his hidden intents will be dominant and visible. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/288-289.\nHow important is the maintaining of righteous hidden intents?\nفَمَا لَهُۥ مِن قُوَّةٖ وَلَا نَاصِرٖ ١٠\nThe disbeliever will have no power to ward off Allah's punishment and His painful torment, nor will he have a helper that can save him from his hardships, as was the case in worldly life when he used to reach for his tribe for protection from anyone who would harm him, or seek an ally who would help him against anyone who would wrong and persecute him. Al-Tabari: 24/359.\nExplain the lack of power and helper for the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection.\nإِنَّهُمۡ يَكِيدُونَ كَيۡدٗا ١٥ وَأَكِيدُ كَيۡدٗا ١٦\nSo that it may be known who will prevail, for humans are too weak and insignificant to be able to resist the Almighty, the All-Knowing and His plans. Al-Saadi: 920.\nThe disbelievers devise plans against the Muslims constantly; who do you think will win in light of this verse?\nوَنُيَسِّرُكَ لِلۡيُسۡرَىٰ ٨\nMeaning: We will make saying and doing good deeds easy for you, and We will ordain such Sharia for you that is easy, tolerant, straight and just with no deviance, difficulty or hardship. Ibn Kathir: 4/501.\nFrom this verse, draw what indicates the tolerance of Islam.\nفَذَكِّرۡ إِن نَّفَعَتِ ٱلذِّكۡرَىٰ ٩\nMeaning: Remind where reminding is beneficial. From here, the etiquette of spreading knowledge is learned. It should not be wasted upon those who are not suitable or worthy of it. Abdullah bin Masoud (t) said, \"You do not tell people any statement that their intellects do not grasp except that it will be a trial for some of them.\" Ali bin Abi Talib (t) said, \"Speak to the people according to their level of understanding. Do you wish that Allah and His Messenger be denied?\" Ibn Kathir: 4/501.\nThis verse (if the reminder should benefit) indicates an etiquette for a preacher. What is it?\nفَذَكِّرۡ إِن نَّفَعَتِ ٱلذِّكۡرَىٰ ٩ سَيَذَّكَّرُ مَن يَخۡشَىٰ ١٠\nFull remembrance entails being affected by the reminder. If one remembers something he loves, he will pursue it, and if he remembers something he fears, he will flee from it. Ibn Taimyah: 6/502.\nRemembrance is linked to the fear of Allah. Why?\nwords\nالثَّاقِبُPiercing brightness\nدَافِقٍGushing forth\nالصُّلبِThe backbone\nوَالتَّرَائِبِChest ribs\nتُبلَى السَّرَائِرُSecrets will be disclosed\nرُوَيدًاFor a while\nالمَرعَىThe pasture\nغُثَاءًChaff\nأَحوَىWithered"],[592,"§Al-A'la, Al-Ghashiyah\ndeeds\nRepeat after the caller to prayer and say the supplication afterward, then go to the mosque for prayer.\nFind something that you like of worldly adornments, and give it to charity.\nRemind a fellow Muslim of Allah.\nguid\nIf you like something but Allah does not, then choose what He likes.\nThe great aim of prayer is establishing the remembrance of Allah, so be keen on that.\nSincerity and acceptance are more important than deeds themselves.\nrefl\nقَدۡ أَفۡلَحَ مَن تَزَكَّىٰ ١٤ وَذَكَرَ ٱسۡمَ رَبِّهِۦ فَصَلَّىٰ ١٥\nPurifying comes before Allah's remembrance and prayer because it is the essence of all deeds, for if the soul is purified, it will shine with the lights of guidance, become aware of their merits and turn often to them. Ibn Ashur: 30/288.\nPurifying comes before Allah's remembrance and prayer. Why?\nبَلۡ تُؤۡثِرُونَ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا ١٦\nThe meaning of preferring the worldly life is being content and satisfied with it, and neglecting the Hereafter completely. Al-Alusi: 15/322.\nWhat is meant by preferring the worldly life ?\nوُجُوهٞ يَوۡمَئِذٍ خَٰشِعَةٌ ٢ عَامِلَةٞ نَّاصِبَةٞ ٣\n(Humbled), humiliated. Initially, they were not described as humiliated, for describing them as humbled implies a ridicule of them, because they were not humbled in worldly life when it would have been beneficial to them. The same thing can be said about describing them as working hard and weary. Al-Alusi: 15/325.\nWhat is the aim of describing the faces of disbelievers as humbled and working hard.\nفِي جَنَّةٍ عَالِيَةٖ ١٠\nDescribing Paradise as (elevated) indicates its beauty because the best of gardens are those which are located over the hills. Ibn Ashur: 30/299.\nParadise is described as (elevated), why?\nلَّا تَسۡمَعُ فِيهَا لَٰغِيَةٗ ١١\nRather, what will be heard in Paradise is Allah's remembrance such as praising, glorifying, and exalting Him, for the splendors within Paradise will inspire such remembrance. Moreover, the hearts of its inhabitants will be cleared of liking to engage in idle talk of what they used to hate to do in worldly life that contrasted with wisdom. Al-Biqai: 22/9.\nIn Paradise, what will be the substitute for idle talk?\nفِيهَا سُرُرٞ مَّرۡفُوعَةٞ ١٣\n(Within it are couches raised high), the couches will be raised high so when the believer sits on them, he can see all that which Allah has given him of bliss and kingdom around him. Al-Tabari: 24/38.\nAllah has made the couches raised high in Paradise. Why?\nأَفَلَا يَنظُرُونَ إِلَى ٱلۡإِبِلِ كَيۡفَ خُلِقَتۡ ١٧\nAllah urges people to reflect on the creation of camels due to their wonders such as their strength, the ease by which it can be led by a weak person, their endurance of thirst with patience, and their many useful benefits such as using them for riding, hauling weights, eating, drinking their milk and urine [for some cases], and akin to it. Ibn Juzay: 2/566.\nList some wonders of the creation of camels.\nwords\nيَصلَى النَّارHe who will enter and burn in the Fire\nعَامِلَةٌ نَاصِبَةٌOverburdened and weary\nآنِيَةٍIntensely hot\nضَرِيعٍBitter thorny plants\nلاَغِيَةًNo ill-speech\nمَوضُوعَةٌPlaced ready for the drinkers\nوَنَمَارِقُCushions\nوَزَرَابِيُّ مَبثُوثَةٌMany carpets spread out\nسُطِحَتSpread out"],[593,"§Al-Fajr, Al-Ghashiyah\ndeeds\nPray Al-Witr prayer.\nHonor an orphan with a gift or kind words.\nGive some of your money to charity to lessen its love in your heart.\nguid\nThe first ten days of the month of Dhul-Hijjah are of great virtue.\nAccepting Allah's Will and Decree is a trait of the believers.\nBe kind to orphans and those in need.\nrefl\nهَلۡ فِي ذَٰلِكَ قَسَمٞ لِّذِي حِجۡرٍ ٥\nMeaning: For he who possesses intellect, sound reasoning, understanding and religious discernment. The intellect has been called \"Hijr\" (a barrier) because it prevents the person from unsuitable actions and words. Ibn Kathir: 4/508.\nWhat is the importance of intellect to a Muslim?\nوَفِرۡعَوۡنَ ذِي ٱلۡأَوۡتَادِ ١٠\nMeaning: Believing that it would not perish, Pharaoh backed his kingdom with troops of soldiers and with other people and things that would support his kingdom until he established his dominance. Al-Biqai: 22/30.\nPharaoh is described as owner of the stakes, then his doom is related. Why?\nفَصَبَّ عَلَيۡهِمۡ رَبُّكَ سَوۡطَ عَذَابٍ ١٣\nIbn Atiyah said: The word \"whip\" is used [in the Arabic text] metaphorically for punishment because it indicates repetition that the sword would not have. Al-Zamakhshari said: The mention of \"whip\" indicates the punishment in worldly life because it is lighter than the punishment in the Hereafter since whipping is a lesser punishment than killing. Ibn Juzay: 2/569.\nUsing the word \"whip\" as a metaphor for punishment has two eloquent aspects. What are they?\nإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَبِٱلۡمِرۡصَادِ ١٤\nIbn Abbas said: He hears and He sees. This means that He watches over His creation in what they do, and He will reward them in this life and the Hereafter based upon what each of them strove for. He will bring all the creation before Him and judge them with justice. He will requite each of them with what he deserves, for He is exalted above injustice. Ibn Kathir: 4/510.\nWhat should be your practical position when you know that Allah is ever Watchful?\nفَأَمَّا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ إِذَا مَا ٱبۡتَلَىٰهُ رَبُّهُۥ فَأَكۡرَمَهُۥ وَنَعَّمَهُۥ فَيَقُولُ رَبِّيٓ أَكۡرَمَنِ ١٥\nThis is a description of the disbeliever who does not believe in resurrection, as he believes that honor is tied to the abundance of wealth, and humiliation is tied to poverty. To the believer, however, true honor is when Allah honors him with obedience to Him and grants him success that enables him to attain the great reward in the Hereafter; and when Allah extends his provision in worldly life, he becomes grateful to Him. Al-Qurtubi: 22/276.\nIs having worldly gains a sign of Allah's honor to the servant?\nفَأَمَّا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ إِذَا مَا ٱبۡتَلَىٰهُ رَبُّهُۥ فَأَكۡرَمَهُۥ وَنَعَّمَهُۥ فَيَقُولُ رَبِّيٓ أَكۡرَمَنِ ١٥ وَأَمَّآ إِذَا مَا ٱبۡتَلَىٰهُ فَقَدَرَ عَلَيۡهِ رِزۡقَهُۥ فَيَقُولُ رَبِّيٓ أَهَٰنَنِ ١٦ كَلَّاۖ\nAllah refutes man in his belief that if Allah gives him abundant provisions to test him with, it is out of His honor for him. But this is not the case, rather, it is a trial and a test. Likewise, from another angle, if Allah tests him and tries him by restricting his provision, he believes that is because Allah is humiliating him. As Allah says, (No indeed), which means that the matter is not as he claims, neither in this nor in that. For indeed Allah gives wealth to those whom He loves as well as those whom He does not love. Likewise, He withholds provision from those whom He loves and those whom He does not love. The point is that Allah should be obeyed in either circumstance. If one is wealthy, he should thank Allah for that, and if he is poor, he should exercise patience. Ibn Kathir: 4/510.\nBoth wealth and poverty can be either blessings or afflictions. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَلَا تَحَٰٓضُّونَ عَلَىٰ طَعَامِ ٱلۡمِسۡكِينِ ١٨\nMeaning: You do not encourage one another to feed the poor who are in need, because of the covetousness and extreme love of worldly gain deeply entrenched in your hearts. Al-Saadi: 924.\nWhat prevents man from feeding the poor and the needy?\nwords\nإِيَابَهُمTheir return after death\nلِذِي حِجرٍOne who reasons\nإِرَمَEram, a tribe in Yemen\nذَاتِ العِمَادِHad power and buildings on lofty pillars\nجَابُواThey carved\nذِي الأَوتَادِOwner of the soldiers\nفَقَدَرَRestricts\nولاَ تَحَآضُّونَYou do not encourage one another\nالتُّرَاثَInheritance\nجَمًّاImmensely"],[594,"§Al-Fajr, Al-Balad\ndeeds\nSay, \"I am pleased with Allah as my Lord, with Islam as my religion, and with Muhammad (ﷺ) as my Prophet.\"\nAsk Allah for a good end to your life.\nExhort those around you to be patient in obeying Allah, refrain patiently from disobeying Him, or endure His decrees patiently. Moreover, exhort them to be compassionate toward others.\nguid\nBe mindful of Allah in private and in public.\nThe city of Makkah holds many virtuous features.\nThe servant should strive against himself in this worldly life.\nrefl\nيَقُولُ يَٰلَيۡتَنِي قَدَّمۡتُ لِحَيَاتِي ٢٤\nMeaning: If he was a disobedient person, he will regret the acts of disobedience he committed, and if he was an obedient person, he will wish that he performed more acts of obedience. Ibn Kathir: 4/511.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, the feeling of regret will not be limited to committing sins. Explain.\nيَٰٓأَيَّتُهَا ٱلنَّفۡسُ ٱلۡمُطۡمَئِنَّةُ ٢٧ ٱرۡجِعِيٓ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكِ رَاضِيَةٗ مَّرۡضِيَّةٗ ٢٨\nMeaning: A tranquil soul is one that reaches certainty in faith beyond any doubt. Moreover, it is said that a tranquil soul will not have fear at that time. Ibn Juzay: 2/572.\nWhat is the quality with which the soul deserves to be pleased?\nلَقَدۡ خَلَقۡنَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ فِي كَبَدٍ ٤\nThis means all hardships that man suffers and goes through in this world, after death (Al-Barzakh), and on the Day of Resurrection. So man should strive hard to do what will bring him relief from these hardships and lead to eternal bliss and joy, for if he does not do that, he will continue to suffer harsh punishment for all eternity. Al-Saadi: 925.\nAre the hardships that man goes through limited to this worldly life? How can he save himself from these hardships?\nيَقُولُ أَهۡلَكۡتُ مَالٗا لُّبَدًا ٦\nAllah describes spending on desires and sins as squandering, because the spender does not benefit from what he spends, and his spending only leads to regret, loss, exhaustion and diminishing of wealth. Al-Saadi: 925.\nThe word (squandered) is used, not \"spent\", why?\nأَلَمۡ نَجۡعَل لَّهُۥ عَيۡنَيۡنِ ٨ وَلِسَانٗا وَشَفَتَيۡنِ ٩ وَهَدَيۡنَٰهُ ٱلنَّجۡدَيۡنِ ١٠\nThese immense blessings entail a person to fulfill his duties toward Allah, be grateful to Him for His blessings, and not use them to disobey Him. Al-Saadi: 925.\nKnowing that Allah had made your eyes, tongue, and lips, and shown you the two ways (good and evil), what should be your viable position toward these blessings?\nفَلَا ٱقۡتَحَمَ ٱلۡعَقَبَةَ ١١ وَمَآ أَدۡرَىٰكَ مَا ٱلۡعَقَبَةُ ١٢\nThe difficult pass refers to the righteous deeds mentioned afterward. The term (difficult pass) is used here to resemble the difficulty of passing over a mountain, which is rigorous and demanding for souls. Ibn Juzay: 2/574.\nRighteous deeds are referred to as (difficult pass). Why?\nيَتِيمٗا ذَا مَقۡرَبَةٍ ١٥\n(Relative), kinship. He is singled out because feeding him is more worthy than others. This is supported by the Prophetic Hadith: \"Giving charity to a poor person is charity, and [giving] to a relative is two things, charity and upholding the ties of kinship.\" Al-Shanqiti: 8/533.\nThe orphan relative is singled out for feeding. Why?\nwords\nوَأَنَّى لَهُ الذِّكرَىWhat good to him will be the remembrance\nوَلاَ يُوثِقُNone will bind with chains and shackles\nوَثَاقَهُHis binding\nلاَ أُقسِمُI swear\nكَبَدٍHardship\nلُبَدًاIn abundance\nالعَقَبَةَThe obstacle to the Hereafter\nمَسغَبَةٍSevere hunger\nذَا مَترَبَةٍIn misery"],[595,"§Ash-Shams, Al-Lail, Al-Balad\ndeeds\nPray two Rak'a for Ad-Duha prayer.\nSay, \"O Allah! Grant me the sense of piety and purify my soul as You are the Best to purify it. You are its Guardian and its Protector.\"\nSay, \"O Allah! Inspire in me guidance and deliver me from the evils within myself.\"\nguid\nAllah's punishment of stubborn disbelievers is immense.\nOne should constantly reform and discipline himself.\nGiving charity for the sake of Allah is a reason for easing life's matters.\nrefl\nوَنَفۡسٖ وَمَا سَوَّىٰهَا ٧\nThe soul is one of the great signs of Allah that deserves to be sworn by, for the soul is extremely subtle and light; it moves about easily, changes easily, and is influenced easily, subject to emotions such as desiring, wanting, aiming, loving and hating. Without the soul, a body would be a mere image, with nothing good in it. The fact that it is created in such a manner is one of the great signs of Allah. Al-Saadi: 926.\nAllah swears by His great creation. What is so great about the soul?\nفَأَلۡهَمَهَا فُجُورَهَا وَتَقۡوَىٰهَا ٨\nMuhammad bin Ka'b said: If Allah is pleased with a servant, He will inspire him to do righteous deeds, and if He is displeased with a servant, He will inspire him to do evil deeds. Al-Qurtubi: 22/312.\nWhat is the sign of Allah's pleasure or displeasure with His servant?\nقَدۡ أَفۡلَحَ مَن زَكَّىٰهَا ٩ وَقَدۡ خَابَ مَن دَسَّىٰهَا ١٠\nMeaning: Whoever raises himself to higher standards through gaining good knowledge and doing righteous deeds, wins every reward and is saved from every harm. And the true loser is the one who puts his soul down and hides it in wickedness through ignorance and rebellion. Al-Alusi: 15/361.\nHow does the human soul succeed?\nفَكَذَّبُوهُ فَعَقَرُوهَا\nMeaning: The most wretched among them hamstrung her, but the action is attributed to all of them because they were content with what he did. Al-Qurtubi: 22/412.\nThe hamstringing was carried out by one person, but it is attributed to all of them. Why?\nوَمَا خَلَقَ ٱلذَّكَرَ وَٱلۡأُنثَىٰٓ ٣\nHere, Allah swears by Himself as the Creator of males and females. As dictated by His wisdom, He created every type of animal that He wanted to survive as male and female, so that the species may survive and not disappear, and he led each of them to the other by means of desire, making each of them suited to the other. Al-Saadi: 927.\nWhat is Allah's wisdom in creating male and female of everything?\nفَأَمَّا مَنۡ أَعۡطَىٰ وَٱتَّقَىٰ ٥ وَصَدَّقَ بِٱلۡحُسۡنَىٰ ٦ فَسَنُيَسِّرُهُۥ لِلۡيُسۡرَىٰ ٧\nMeaning: We will make him take the easy path, which is doing the good and refraining from evil. The opposite of that is making him take the hard path. This is supported by the Prophetic Hadith: \"Strive, for it will be made easy for each person to do that for which he was created.\" Meaning: Allah will make smooth for him the path that was decreed for him, and ease him toward doing good or doing evil. Ibn Juzay: 2/589.\nIn light of this verse, explain the Prophet's Hadith: \"Strive, for it will be made easy for each person to do that for which he was created.\"\nفَأَمَّا مَنۡ أَعۡطَىٰ وَٱتَّقَىٰ ٥ وَصَدَّقَ بِٱلۡحُسۡنَىٰ ٦ فَسَنُيَسِّرُهُۥ لِلۡيُسۡرَىٰ ٧\nSome of the righteous predecessors said: A reward for a good deed is making another good deed afterward, and a recompense for an evil deed is making another evil deed afterward. Ibn Kathir: 4/520.\nIn light of these verses, explain the statement mentioned above.\nwords\nمُؤصَدَةٌClosed shut\nطَحَاهَاHe who spread it\nدَسَّاهَاHe who corrupts it\nفَعَقَرُوهَاThey hamstrung her\nفَدَمدَمَHe brought down destruction upon them\nتَجَلَّىIt appears with its light\nلَشَتَّىDiverse"],[596,"§Al-Lail, Ad-Duha\ndeeds\nSpend some of your wealth for charity, even if little.\nPray two Rak'a for Ad-Duha prayer.\nBe kind to an orphan.\nguid\nBe keen to purify yourself.\nAbundance of wealth will not avail a denier from the punishment.\nSeek the reward from Allah, and do not look for a praise from people.\nrefl\nٱلَّذِي يُؤۡتِي مَالَهُۥ يَتَزَكَّىٰ ١٨ وَمَا لِأَحَدٍ عِندَهُۥ مِن نِّعۡمَةٖ تُجۡزَىٰٓ ١٩\nThis verse contains guidance to the righteous that he should not be accepting favors from others and endure their reminders, but if he does, then, he should hasten to requite them so that he is free of their favors, and his deeds become completely devoted to Allah, not as a return for favors. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/326.\nWhat should the righteous do when he receives favors from others? Why?\nوَمَا لِأَحَدٍ عِندَهُۥ مِن نِّعۡمَةٖ تُجۡزَىٰٓ ١٩ إِلَّا ٱبۡتِغَآءَ وَجۡهِ رَبِّهِ ٱلۡأَعۡلَىٰ ٢٠ وَلَسَوۡفَ يَرۡضَىٰ ٢١\nMeaning: He should not do a good deed as a return for someone's favors in the past, rather, from the outset, he should do it for the sake of Allah. Ibn Juzay: 2/580.\nAllah makes a condition for the spender to receive His pleasure. What is it?\nمَا وَدَّعَكَ رَبُّكَ وَمَا قَلَىٰ ٣ وَلَلۡأٓخِرَةُ خَيۡرٞ لَّكَ مِنَ ٱلۡأُولَىٰ ٤\nMeaning: The Hereafter is better for you than the present life, and you chose the former over the latter, and therefore, your Lord will never forsake you. This serves as a guidance to the believers to that which brings them closer to Allah, and a rebuke to the polytheists for clinging to this worldly life and turning away from the Hereafter. Al-Alusi: 15/379.\nWhat is the quality of a servant who is close to his Lord? Explain in light of this verse.\nوَأَمَّا ٱلسَّآئِلَ فَلَا تَنۡهَرۡ ١٠\nThis includes those who ask for money and those who ask for knowledge. Hence, teachers are enjoined to treat learners kindly, gently and with compassion, for this will help the learner to achieve his goal, and it reflects kindness toward the one who is striving to benefit the people and the homeland. Al-Saadi: 928.\nIs the prohibited repulsion limited to a beggar who asks for money only? Explain.\nوَأَمَّا بِنِعۡمَةِ رَبِّكَ فَحَدِّثۡ ١١\nSpeaking of the blessings of Allah prompts one to give thanks for them, and leads to the love of the One Who bestowed those blessings, for people are naturally inclined to love the one who does favors. Al-Saadi: 929.\nHow can speaking of the blessings of Allah become a reason for increasing the faith?\nوَأَمَّا بِنِعۡمَةِ رَبِّكَ فَحَدِّثۡ ١١\nSpeaking about Allah's blessings is in itself showing gratitude for them. Some righteous predecessors liked for one to speak about his good deeds, without intending to show off, if he knew that others may emulate him. Al-Alusi: 15/383.\nThe believers are enjoined to speak about Allah's blessings. Why?\nأَلَمۡ نَشۡرَحۡ لَكَ صَدۡرَكَ ١\nThe breast is singled out for mention because it is the place of awareness and cognition. Meaning: Reminding the Prophet (ﷺ) of opening and expanding his breast so that he could convey the Message, and carry out the burden of Prophethood and preserving the revelation. Al-Shawkani: 5/461.\nThe breast is singled out for mention in this verse, why? What is meant by that?\nwords\nلِلعُسرَىToward difficulty\nوَمَا يُغنِيIt will be of no avail to him\nتَرَدَّىFalls into the Fire\nإِنَّ عَلَينَا لَلهُدَىIt is upon Us to show the right way\nتَلَظَّىBlazing\nلاَ يَصلاَهَاNone will enter it\nوَسَيُجَنَّبُهَاWill be saved from it\nسَجَىCovers with darkness\nوَمَا قَلَىNor has He detested you\nفَآوَىHe has given you refuge and good care\nعَائِلًاPoor"],[597,"§Ash-Sharh, Al-Alaq, At-Tin\ndeeds\nUse part of your free time for worship.\nRead two pages from an Islamic reference book.\nSupplicat Allah to teach you what benefits you and to increase your knowledge.\nguid\nFaith and righteous deeds preserve one's honor with Allah.\nBe keen to submit and adhere to the rules of Islam.\nReading is important in the life of a Muslim.\nrefl\nفَإِنَّ مَعَ ٱلۡعُسۡرِ يُسۡرًا ٥ إِنَّ مَعَ ٱلۡعُسۡرِ يُسۡرٗا ٦\nEven though the word (hardship) is repeated twice, however, in the Arabic text, it is in a definite form which makes it one thing, while the word for (ease) is repeated in an indefinite form which makes it two things. Hardship is bounded by two forms of ease; one before and one after. Hence, a single hardship will never defeat two forms of ease. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/333.\nEase is much wider than hardship. Explain in light of these two verses.\nلَقَدۡ خَلَقۡنَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ فِيٓ أَحۡسَنِ تَقۡوِيمٖ ٤\n(The best form): Is his body proportion and perfect youthfulness. Abu Bakr bin Tahir said: \"Man is adorned with intellect, performs what is required of him, guided by his sound judgment, stands upright, and eats his food with his hand.\" He is Allah's best creation inwardly and outwardly due to the beauty of his form, the shape of his head and what it consists of, his chest and what it holds, his belly and what it contains, his hands and how they strike, and his feet and how they carry him. Al-Qurtubi: 22/368-369.\nAllah reminds man that He created him in the best form. Why? What are the examples of that?\nثُمَّ رَدَدۡنَٰهُ أَسۡفَلَ سَٰفِلِينَ ٥\nFrom the context, the apparent meaning of this verse indicates the status of the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection, where his image will be most hideous and ugly after it was the most beautiful and in the best shape because of his ungratefulness to Allah for His blessing. Al-Alusi: 30/176.\nWho will be returned to the lowest of the low?\nأَلَيۡسَ ٱللَّهُ بِأَحۡكَمِ ٱلۡحَٰكِمِينَ ٨\nMeaning: Is He not the Most Just of all judges Who does not oppress or do any injustice to anyone? Part of His justice is that He will establish the Day of Resurrection, where He will give retribution to the person who was wronged in this life against whoever wronged him. Ibn Kathir: 4/529.\nThis verse proves the resurrection and recompense. How?\nٱقۡرَأۡ وَرَبُّكَ ٱلۡأَكۡرَمُ ٣ ٱلَّذِي عَلَّمَ بِٱلۡقَلَمِ ٤\nAmong the methods of teachings is teaching by the pen, which is writing, is singled out for mention because it preserves knowledge and keeps records of religious and worldly affairs. Ibn Juzay: 2/590.\nTeaching by the pen is singled out for mention. Why?\nٱقۡرَأۡ وَرَبُّكَ ٱلۡأَكۡرَمُ ٣ ٱلَّذِي عَلَّمَ بِٱلۡقَلَمِ ٤ عَلَّمَ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ مَا لَمۡ يَعۡلَمۡ ٥\nAllah honored man by giving him knowledge, which was the distinguishing status that the Father of Humanity, Adam (u), had over the angels. Ibn Kathir: 4/530.\nWhat is the status that distinguishes Adam (u) and his descendants over the other created beings?\nكَلَّآ إِنَّ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ لَيَطۡغَىٰٓ ٦ أَن رَّءَاهُ ٱسۡتَغۡنَىٰٓ ٧ إِنَّ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ ٱلرُّجۡعَىٰٓ ٨\nAllah states that when a person sees himself as self-sufficient and having an abundance of wealth, he becomes pleased, evil, scornful, and transgressive. Then, Allah threatens, warns and admonishes him by saying: (Indeed, to your Lord is the return), unto Allah is the final destination and return, and He will hold you accountable for your wealth, as to from where you obtained it and how did you spend it. Ibn Kathir: 4/531.\nWhen a person becomes self-sufficient, what must he do?\nwords\nأَنقَضَWeighed down\nفَرَغتَWhen you finished your worldly affairs\nفَانصَبStrive in worship\nفَارغَبTurn in devotion\nوَطُورِ سِينِينَMount Sinai where Allah spoke to Moses (u)\nوَهَذَا البَلَدِMakkah\nتَقوِيمٍImage, form\nغَيرُ مَمنُونٍUninterrupted, and never ends\nعَلَقٍA clinging clot\nالرُّجعَىThe final return"],[598,"§Al-Alaq, Al-Bayyinah, Al-Qadr\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, lead me to righteousness and piety.\"\nBecome nearer to Allah through prostration, either in prayer, for thanking Him, or while reciting the Quran.\nRemind those around you of the importance of sincerity in worship.\nguid\nThe virtue of the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr) and its good events is immense.\nEnsure unity and adherence to the book of Allah (the Quran) and the Sunnah of His Messenger, and reject division.\nThe best deeds after Tawhīd are prayer, which is a duty to Allah, and zakah, which is a duty to people.\nrefl\nإِنَّآ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ فِي لَيۡلَةِ ٱلۡقَدۡرِ ١\nThe fact that the Quran was revealed at night is indicative of the virtue of the night. The Quran and Prophetic Sunnah have indications of this meaning. From the Quran: (Glory be to the One Who took His servant by night), (And pray from the night), (And glorify Him in the night and after prostration), (Indeed, worship at night is more effective), and (They used to sleep only a little at night). From Prophetic Sunnah: \"Our Lord who is blessed and exalted descends every night to the lowest heaven when the last one-third of the night remains.\" This indicates that the night is the time for divine inspiration and the nearness of the Lord to His servants, as the heart is clear of distractions. The stillness and awe of the night make the heart clearer and more attentive. Al-Shanqiti: 9/38.\nThe Quran was revealed at night, not during the day. Why?\nإِنَّآ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ فِي لَيۡلَةِ ٱلۡقَدۡرِ ١\nIn this verse, the pronoun refers to the Quran, which venerates the Quran in three aspect: First: Referring to the Quran using a pronoun rather than its name indicates that it is well known. Second: Selecting the best time to send it down, which is the night. Third: Allah attributes the sending of the Quran to Himself. Ibn Juzay: 2/593.\nThis verse venerates the Quran in three aspects. Explain.\nلَمۡ يَكُنِ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ مِنۡ أَهۡلِ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ وَٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ مُنفَكِّينَ حَتَّىٰ تَأۡتِيَهُمُ ٱلۡبَيِّنَةُ ١\nThe people of the Book are mentioned before the polytheists because of their knowledge which should have guided them to the truth, but this reflects their crookedness and stubbornness. Al-Biqai: 22/192.\nThe people of the Book are mentioned before the polytheists. Why?\nوَمَا تَفَرَّقَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ إِلَّا مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا جَآءَتۡهُمُ ٱلۡبَيِّنَةُ ٤\nAfter being mentioned with others at the beginning of the Surah, the people of the Book are singled out for mention here because they knew the truthfulness of our Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ), as he is mentioned in their scriptures. Ibn Juzay: 2/597.\nAfter being mentioned with others at the beginning of the Surah, the people of the Book are singled out for mention in this verse. Why?\nوَمَآ أُمِرُوٓاْ إِلَّا لِيَعۡبُدُواْ ٱللَّهَ مُخۡلِصِينَ لَهُ ٱلدِّينَ حُنَفَآءَ وَيُقِيمُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَيُؤۡتُواْ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَۚ وَذَٰلِكَ دِينُ ٱلۡقَيِّمَةِ ٥\n(Although they were commanded only to worship Allah with sincere devotion to Him, being inclined to the true faith), avoiding shirk and being inclined to Tawhīd. (And to establish prayer), which is the most honored form of physical worship. (And give zakah), which is doing good to the poor and the needy. (That is the true religion), the upright and just religion, or the nation that is straight and balanced. Many scholars, such as Al-Zuhri and Al-Shafi'i quoted this verse to prove that deeds are part of faith. Ibn Kathir: 4/540.\nHow does this verse prove the belief of Ahl Al-Sunnah that faith is: A belief within the heart, speech by the tongue, and physical actions?\nوَمَآ أُمِرُوٓاْ إِلَّا لِيَعۡبُدُواْ ٱللَّهَ مُخۡلِصِينَ لَهُ ٱلدِّينَ حُنَفَآءَ وَيُقِيمُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَيُؤۡتُواْ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَۚ وَذَٰلِكَ دِينُ ٱلۡقَيِّمَةِ ٥\nAllah singles out prayer and zakah for mention, even though they are included in these words (to worship Allah with sincere devotion to Him), because of their special virtue and because they are the two acts of worship which, if anyone undertakes them, he will undertake all other religious duties. Al-Saadi: 932.\nAllah singles out prayer and zakah for mention, even though they are included in worship?\nوَمَآ أُمِرُوٓاْ إِلَّا لِيَعۡبُدُواْ ٱللَّهَ مُخۡلِصِينَ لَهُ ٱلدِّينَ حُنَفَآءَ\nThis verse proves that intention is obligatory when performing acts of worship. Sincerity is a deed of the heart, which is a complete devotion to Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 22/412.\nThis verse proves an important principle. What is it?\nwords\nلَنَسفَعًاWe will surely drag him to the Fire\nنَادِيَهُHis council [of helpers]\nالزَّبَانِيَةَAngels of Hell\nمُنفَكِّينَDesist from disbelief\nكُتُبٌ قَيِّمَةٌTrue narrations and just laws"],[599,"§Az-Zalzalah, Al-Bayyinah, Al-Adiyat\ndeeds\nPray in a spot that you like, so it will bear witness for you on the Day of Resurrection.\nTonight, reckon with yourself over good deeds and evil ones up until now.\nSmile at your Muslim brother and remove obstacles from people's paths, as these good deeds require little effort to do but are greatly rewarded.\nguid\nPeople of faith and righteous deeds are the best of creatures.\nThe horrors of the Day of Resurrection will be immense.\nMostly, death comes at an unexpected time.\nrefl\nرَّضِيَ ٱللَّهُ عَنۡهُمۡ وَرَضُواْ عَنۡهُۚ\nThere will not be a wish that Allah does not grant them even though they are aware of His overall bounty. Allah, the Almighty, is not obligated to do anything for anyone, and no one reveres Him His true reverence. If He were to take people to task for their wrongdoing, they would be doomed. The greatest blessing he bestowed upon them was making them the followers of His Messenger, and that was the cause of all the good they receive. Al-Biqai: 22/198.\nWhat is the meaning of (and they are pleased with Him)?\nجَزَآؤُهُمۡ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ جَنَّٰتُ عَدۡنٖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَآ أَبَدٗاۖ رَّضِيَ ٱللَّهُ عَنۡهُمۡ وَرَضُواْ عَنۡهُۚ ذَٰلِكَ لِمَنۡ خَشِيَ رَبَّهُۥ ٨\nFear of Allah is the basis of true happiness and a means to attain high ranks with Allah, without which no one will refrain from sins or become ready for a day when people are seized by their forelocks and their feet. Al-Alusi: 15/431.\nWhat is the meaning of the fear of Allah?\nجَزَآؤُهُمۡ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ جَنَّٰتُ عَدۡنٖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَآ أَبَدٗاۖ رَّضِيَ ٱللَّهُ عَنۡهُمۡ وَرَضُواْ عَنۡهُۚ ذَٰلِكَ لِمَنۡ خَشِيَ رَبَّهُۥ ٨\nWhoever fears his Lord as such, will abstain from everything that is unsuitable for Allah's Majesty, and will not revile or reject His Message. A heart devoid of fear is a ruined one. Al-Biqai: 22/199.\nWhat is the sign of the servant's fear of Allah?\nيَوۡمَئِذٖ تُحَدِّثُ أَخۡبَارَهَا ٤\nThe earth will testify concerning people and what they did on its surface of good or evil. The earth will be among the witnesses who will testify concerning people's deeds. Al-Saadi: 932.\nWhat is the practical behavior we learn from this verse?\nيَوْمَىِٕذٍ يَّصْدُرُ النَّاسُ اَشْتَاتًا لِّيُرَوْا اَعْمَالَهُمْۗ ٦\nWhen witnessing the recompense on the Day of Resurrection, everyone will be blaming himself. If he is a doer of good, will say: Why did I not increase my good deeds? And if is otherwise, will say: Why did I not refrain from sins? Ibn Abbas said: They will be separated into groups according to their deeds. Al-Qurtubi: 22/437.\nWhat is the wisdom behind showing people their deeds on the Day of Resurrection?\nفَمَن يَعۡمَلۡ مِثۡقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ خَيۡرٗا يَرَهُۥ ٧ وَمَن يَعۡمَلۡ مِثۡقَالَ ذَرَّةٖ شَرّٗا يَرَهُۥ ٨\nThe atom is a tiny ant. (Will see it), he will be recompensed for it. The mention of an atom's weight is to indicate that he will surely be recompensed for what is bigger than that; as if saying: Whoever does a little or plenty, will be recompensed for it. Ibn Juzay: 2/600.\nWhat does the mention of an atom's weight indicate?\nفَمَن يَعۡمَلۡ مِثۡقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ خَيۡرٗا يَرَهُۥ ٧ وَمَن يَعۡمَلۡ مِثۡقَالَ ذَرَّةٖ شَرّٗا يَرَهُۥ ٨\nAnas narrated that Allah's Messenger said: \"Allah does not wrong a believer any of his good deeds because he is given provision for them in this world and will be rewarded for them in the Hereafter. The disbeliever, however, is given in the world the reward for good deeds, but on the Day of Resurrection, there will be no good deeds for which he can be rewarded.\" Al-Tabari: 24/553.\nAllah is Just Who does not wrong anyone; the disbeliever who does good deeds will not find his deeds on the Day of Resurrection. How?\nwords\nيَصدُرُ النَّاسُPeople will come forward\nأَشتَاتًاSeparate groups\nوَالعَادِيَاتِ ضَبحًاBy the galloping, panting horses\nفَالمُورِيَاتِ قَدحًاStriking sparks of fire [with their hooves]\nفَالمُغِيرَاتِ صُبحًاLaunching raids at dawn\nفَأَثَرنَStirring up\nنَقعًاDust\nفَوَسَطنَ بِهِ جَمعًاPlunging thereby into the midst of the enemy"],[600,"§Al-Adiyat, Al-Qari'ah, At-Takathur\ndeeds\nGive to charity out of something you love\nIncrease the weight on your Scale of good deeds by doing righteous deeds today.\nVisit the cemetery, as it is a reminder of the Hereafter.\nguid\nBeware of denying Allah's blessings.\nMinding the deeds of the hearts is crucial.\nWorldly life should not distract the servant from his religious duties.\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ لِرَبِّهِۦ لَكَنُودٞ ٦\n(Indeed, man is very ungrateful to his Lord), ungrateful for the blessings that Allah has bestowed upon him and denies them. The meaning of this verse applies to all of mankind because it is part of man's nature to do so, except for those whom Allah has protected through His kindness and enabled them to succeed. Al-Alusi: 15/445.\nWhat would you do now that you know that the majority of people are ungrateful to Allah?\nوَإِنَّهُۥ لِحُبِّ ٱلۡخَيۡرِ لَشَدِيدٌ ٨\nMeaning: Man loves wealth very much, and it is his love thereof that led him not to carry out the duties that he should and to give precedence to his desire for wealth over the dues of his Lord. All of that is because he is short-sighted, limits his focus on this world, and is heedless of the Hereafter. Al-Saadi: 933.\nWhat are the effects of extreme love of wealth on a person's moral behaviors?\n۞أَفَلَا يَعۡلَمُ إِذَا بُعۡثِرَ مَا فِي ٱلۡقُبُورِ ٩ وَحُصِّلَ مَا فِي ٱلصُّدُورِ ١٠\nIn these two verses, Allah mentions graves and hearts together. Man's heart hides within it goodness and evil, and the grave hides within it his body. Then, Allah will bring out the person's body from his grave and bring out the secrets that reside within his heart, so his body will be visible on the earth and his secrets are apparent on his face. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/352-353.\nWhy are hearts and graves mentioned in the same context?\nأَلۡهَىٰكُمُ ٱلتَّكَاثُرُ ١\nThis verse contains an admonishment and a rebuke. (Alhakum), distracts you. (At-Takathur), flaunting with wealth and the number of children, where some would say: \"We have more\", while others would say the same. When the Prophet (ﷺ) read this verse, he said: \"The son of Adam says: 'My wealth, my wealth', and the Prophet said: You will have none of your wealth except that which you ate and it became consumed, or what you wore and it became ragged, or what you gave to charity and it would be stored for you [as a reward in the Hereafter].\" Ibn Juzay: 2/605.\nWhat is intended meaning behind this verse? Include some examples of flaunting.\nأَلۡهَىٰكُمُ ٱلتَّكَاثُرُ ١\nWhat they compete in is not specified, so as to include everything that people compete to accumulate and boast about, such as accumulating wealth, children, supporters, troops, servants, status and other things that people usually compete with one another for, where the aim is not to sincerely seek the pleasure of Allah. Al-Saadi: 933.\nThe verse does not specify what people compete for. Why?\nحَتَّىٰ زُرۡتُمُ ٱلۡمَقَابِرَ ٢\nQatada said: \"They used to say: We outnumber the people of so-and-so tribe, and we own more things than so-and-so tribe, while they were dying every day until they all ended up in the graves.\" Al-Qurtubi: 22/449-450.\nWhat awaits boastful people at the end?\nثُمَّ لَتُسۡـَٔلُنَّ يَوۡمَئِذٍ عَنِ ٱلنَّعِيمِ ٨\nMeaning: You will be asked about your gratefulness towards Allah's blessings; a believer is obligated to thank Allah for the blessings that he was given. Ibn Taimyah: 7/178.\nHow can the believer protect himself from being questioned about his worldly pleasures?\nwords\nلَكَنُودٌUngrateful\nلَشَهِيدٌHe himself is a witness to that\nالخَيرِWealth\nبُعثِرَIs scattered and overturned\nالمَبثُوثِScattered about\nكَالعِهنِWool with different dyes\nالمَنفُوشِCarded, about to disintegrate\nفَأُمُّهُ هَاوِيَةٌHis abode will be the abyss\nعِلمَ اليَقِينِKnowledge of certainty\nعَينَ اليَقِينِYou will see Hellfire with absolute certainty"],[601,"§Al-Humazah, Al-Fil, Al-Asr\ndeeds\nRecall any scorning or mockery you committed and repent.\nSpend some of your wealth for charity.\nExplain to your friends that no matter how arrogant and overwhelming the disbelievers may be, their schemes will turn against them.\nguid\nReflect on the importance of time, as it allows you to reap what you sow in the Hereafter.\nOne of the signs of virtuous brotherhood is exhorting one another to the truth and patience.\nDo not be deluded by your wealth, lest it distracts you from worshiping Allah.\nrefl\nوَٱلۡعَصۡرِ ١ إِنَّ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ لَفِي خُسۡرٍ ٢ إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوۡاْ بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوۡاْ بِٱلصَّبۡرِ ٣\nAl-Shafi'i (t) said: If all the people pondered upon this Surah, it would suffice them. This Surah has four stages through which a person has to go to reach perfection; they are: Knowing the truth, abiding by the truth, teaching it to those who do not know it, and being patient with learning it, abiding by it, and teaching it to others. Hence, Allah mentions these four stages in this Surah. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/365.\nThis Surah contained everything a person needs to be reformed. Explain.\nإِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوۡاْ بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوۡاْ بِٱلصَّبۡرِ ٣\nIn the Arabic text, the word (righteous deeds) is in the definite form, which indicates that they have done all the good deeds that Allah has commanded, and that includes refraining from sins as well. Ibn Ashur: 30/532.\nIn the Arabic text, the word (righteous deeds) is in the definite form. Why?\nإِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوۡاْ بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوۡاْ بِٱلصَّبۡرِ\nBy means of the first two, one may perfect oneself, and by means of the last two, one may help others to perfect themselves. By perfecting all four things, one will be safe from loss and will attain great success. Al-Saadi: 934.\nThese four attributes of the believers are singled out for mention. Why?\nوَتَوَاصَوۡاْ بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوۡاْ بِٱلصَّبۡرِ ٣\n([Exhort one another to patience], be patient when facing calamities, destinies, and the harms of those who harm people due to their commanding them to do good and forbidding them from evil. Ibn Kathir: 4/551.\nWhy was exhorting one another to patience mentioned after exhorting one another to the truth? Explain the relationship between the two.\nٱلَّذِي جَمَعَ مَالٗا وَعَدَّدَهُۥ ٢\nThe aim of this verse is to rebuke those who withhold their wealth and not spend it in the cause of Allah's obedience. Al-Qurtubi: 22/471.\nIs amassing wealth always a vilified behavior?\nيَحۡسَبُ أَنَّ مَالَهُۥٓ أَخۡلَدَهُۥ ٣\nMeaning: A person's wealth makes him believe that he reached the status of immortality in life, which leads him to love his wealth as much as he loves immortality. Hence, he indulged himself in his desires as if he were immortal. Moreover, this implies that immortality is useless without righteous deeds that are beneficial in the Hereafter. Al-Biqai: 22/245.\nClinging excessively to one's own wealth poses a risk to a person's outlook on life. Explain in light of this verse.\nٱلَّتِي تَطَّلِعُ عَلَى ٱلۡأَفۡـِٔدَةِ ٧\nThe hearts are singled out for mention even though the Fire will cover all of their bodies because that is where their false beliefs reside, or because if pain reaches the hearts then they will die. Meaning: They are in a state of dying without ever dying. Al-Shawkani: 5/494.\nThe hearts are singled out for mention even though the Fire will cover all of their bodies. Why?\nwords\nهُمَزَةٍScorner\nلُمَزَةٍMocker\nوَعَدَّدَهُCounts it repeatedly\nلَيُنبَذَنَّSurely he will be thrown\nالحُطَمَةِReaches their hearts\nتَطَّلِعُ عَلَى الأَفئِدَةِReaches their hearts\nمُؤصَدَةٌSealed\nفِي عَمَدٍ مُمَدَّدَةٍLocked with towering columns\nأَبَابِيلَSuccessive flocks of birds"],[602,"§Quraysh, Al-Ma'un, Al-Kawthar\ndeeds\nBe grateful to Allah for the availability of food, water, and security.\nEncourage those around you to feed the poor.\nLend a fellow Muslim what he needs of what you can afford.\nguid\nThe Creator and the Provider is the One Who is worthy of worship.\nBeware of becoming one of those.\nDetesting the Prophet (ﷺ) or any of his message is a grave sin.\nrefl\nفَلۡيَعۡبُدُواْ رَبَّ هَٰذَا ٱلۡبَيۡتِ ٣ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَطۡعَمَهُم مِّن جُوعٖ وَءَامَنَهُم مِّنۡ خَوۡفِۢ ٤\nAllah perished whoever intended evil against the people of Quraish, and glorified the Ka'bah and the people of Makkah within the hearts of the Arabs until they showed respect and did not object to any travels the people of Quraish wanted to do; that is why Allah ordered the people of Quraish to show gratitude, saying: (Let them worship the Lord of this house), they should worship only Allah and should do so with sincerity. Al-Saadi: 894.\nThe Oneness of Allah is a form of gratitude. Explain in light of this Surah.\nٱلَّذِيٓ أَطۡعَمَهُم مِّن جُوعٖ وَءَامَنَهُم مِّنۡ خَوۡفِۢ ٤\nThe combination of both prosperity and security is a great favor from Allah, because a person will not be satisfied or enjoy life unless he is blessed with these two blessings simultaneously; as there is no life with hunger, and no sense of security when fear is present, and only after these blessings are combined will Allah's favor be complete. A-Shanqiti: 9/112.\nWhat was the purpose of simultaneously blessing Quraish with prosperity and security?\nأَرَءَيۡتَ ٱلَّذِي يُكَذِّبُ بِٱلدِّينِ ١ فَذَٰلِكَ ٱلَّذِي يَدُعُّ ٱلۡيَتِيمَ ٢\nLook at those who deny the Recompense, and you will find within them these repulsive behaviors and acts of evil, for faith encourages the believers to do good deeds and refrain from bad ones. Ibn Juzay: 2/614.\nAllah shows that the deniers of the Recompense have repulsive behaviors, why?\nفَوَيۡلٞ لِّلۡمُصَلِّينَ ٤ ٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ عَن صَلَاتِهِمۡ سَاهُونَ ٥\nMeaning: They are those people who pray and adhere to the prayer, yet they are mindless of it. This may either be referring to its act entirely, or it may be referring to performing it in its designated time, which means that the person performs it completely beyond its designated time. Ibn Kathir: 4/558.\nIn what way can someone be heedless of their prayers?\nفَصَلِّ لِرَبِّكَ وَٱنۡحَرۡ ٢\nThe reason that Allah mentions prayer before sacrifice when he says, (So pray to your Lord and offer sacrifice), and why He mentions zakah before prayer when he says, (Indeed, he who purifies himself will attain success ` and remembers his Lord's Name and prays) because part of the Sunnah is to make fast-breaking charity (Zakat Al-Fitr) before prayer in Eid Al-Fitr, and the sacrifice comes after the prayer in Eid Al-Adha. Ibn Taimyah: 7/194.\nWhy is it part of the Sunnah to make the Zakat Al-Fitr before prayer in Eid Al-Fitr, and the sacrifice after the prayer in Eid Al-Adha?\nإِنَّ شَانِئَكَ هُوَ ٱلۡأَبۡتَرُ ٣\nIf a person, openly, commits an offense punishable by Allah, then it is obligatory to punish him and apply Allah's fair rule. It is our duty to break off with those who display hostility and enmity. Ibn Taimyah: 7/196.\nWhat is the difference between one who commits sins openly and another who hides them?\nإِنَّ شَانِئَكَ هُوَ ٱلۡأَبۡتَرُ ٣\nThe people of the Sunnah die, yet their teachings live on, while the innovators (of religious matters) die and so do their teachings, because the people of the Sunnah revitalize the teachings of the Prophet (ﷺ) and therefore became associated with the verse: (And raised high for you your repute), while the innovators hated the teachings of the Prophet (ﷺ) and therefore became associated with the verse: (Indeed, your enemy is truly cut off). Ibn Taimyah: 7/198.\nWhy did the teachings of the Sunnah remain while the teachings of the innovators perished?\nwords\nلإِيلاَفِ قُرَيشٍFor the accustomed security of the Quraysh\nرِحلَةَ الشِّتَاءِWinter travel [to Yemen]\nيَدُعُّ اليَتِيمَDrives the orphan away from his rights\nسَاهُونَNot concerned about prayer; they delay it, and they do not perform it appropriately\nشَانِئَكَYour enemy\nالأَبتَرُOne who is cut off from all goodness"],[603,"§Al-Kafirun, An-Nasr, Al-Masad\ndeeds\nRead Surat Al-Kafirun in the first Rak'a and Surah Al-Ikhlas in the second Rak'a of Al-Fajr and Al-Maghrib's Sunnah prayers.\nInvite a disbeliever to Islam in any way you can.\nSay, \"Glorified is Allah and praised is He\" a hundred times, and ask often for forgiveness.\nguid\nThere is a great risk in weakening religious principles and offering compromises.\nGlorifying Allah and seeking His forgiveness are very important when concluding acts of worship.\nBeware of harming the righteous servants of Allah.\nrefl\nوَلَآ أَنتُمۡ عَٰبِدُونَ مَآ أَعۡبُدُ ٣\nMeaning: Due to your lack of sincerity toward Allah in worshiping Him because your worship of Him is accompanied by polytheism and is not truly deemed as worship. Al-Saadi: 936.\nIt is known that the disbelievers of Quraish used to worship Allah and would worship other deities, then for what purpose did this verse deny their worship to Allah?\nلَكُمۡ دِينُكُمۡ وَلِيَ دِينِ ٦\nImam Abu Abdullah Al-Shafi'i and other scholars deduced from this verse that disbelief of all kinds is one religion, for all religions except Islam are equally null. Ibn Kathir: 4/565.\n\"Disbelief is one religion.\" Explain this statement in light of this verse.\nلَكُمۡ دِينُكُمۡ وَلِيَ دِينِ ٦\nThis Surah adopts a reformist approach by which no half-solutions are ever accepted because the deal that the polytheists offered the Prophet (ﷺ) which aimed to merge people's worship is a compromise; so that each side has a chance of being sided with the truth, but the response was decisive and rebuking, because if the Prophet were to accept their deal for even a moment, it will equalize the truth with falsehood, hold back the issue, and validate falsehood. Al-Shanqiti: 9/136.\nAre half-solutions acceptable in the basics of Islam?\nإِذَا جَآءَ نَصۡرُ ٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡفَتۡحُ ١ وَرَأَيۡتَ ٱلنَّاسَ يَدۡخُلُونَ فِي دِينِ ٱللَّهِ أَفۡوَاجٗا ٢ فَسَبِّحۡ بِحَمۡدِ رَبِّكَ وَٱسۡتَغۡفِرۡهُۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ تَوَّابَۢا ٣\nThis indicates that divine support for this religion would continue and increase when His Messenger (ﷺ) glorified and praised his Lord, and sought His forgiveness, for that is part of gratitude, as Allah says elsewhere, (If you are grateful, I will certainly give you more) [14:7]. Indeed, that came to pass during the time of the Rightly-Guided Caliphs and afterwards. Divine help for this Ummah continued and Islam attained success unmatched by any other religion until the Ummah's attitude changed, and they began to behave contrary to Allah's commands. Then Allah inflicted upon them division and disunity, and there happened what happened. Al-Saadi: 936.\nExplain the importance of glorifying Allah, expressing gratitude, and seeking forgiveness when it comes to helping the nation and religion of Islam.\nإِذَا جَآءَ نَصۡرُ ٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡفَتۡحُ ١ وَرَأَيۡتَ ٱلنَّاسَ يَدۡخُلُونَ فِي دِينِ ٱللَّهِ أَفۡوَاجٗا ٢ فَسَبِّحۡ بِحَمۡدِ رَبِّكَ وَٱسۡتَغۡفِرۡهُۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ تَوَّابَۢا ٣\nIt is known that virtuous matters end with pleas for forgiveness, as in the case of prayer, Hajj and other acts of worship. So, Allah's command to His Messenger (ﷺ) to praise Him and seek His forgiveness in this situation was a hint that his life was coming to an end, so let him prepare and get ready to meet his Lord, and end his life with the best deeds that he could do, (ﷺ). Al-Saadi: 936.\nHow does this Surah indicate the Prophet's (ﷺ) life is nearing its end?\nتَبَّتۡ يَدَآ أَبِي لَهَبٖ وَتَبَّ ١\nFrom this verse, it is known that merely relating to righteous people is not sufficient unless they are emulated, as Abu Lahab is the uncle of the Prophet (ﷺ). Al-Biqai: 22/331.\nDoes one's status of kinship matter if he lacks worship? Explain in light of this verse.\nوَٱمۡرَأَتُهُۥ حَمَّالَةَ ٱلۡحَطَبِ ٤ فِي جِيدِهَا حَبۡلٞ مِّن مَّسَدِۢ ٥\nAbu Lahab's wife supported his disbelief, denial, and obstinacy. Therefore, she will be helping to administer his punishment in the Hellfire, thus, Allah says, (the carrier of firewood ` Around her neck is a rope of [twisted] fiber), which means that she will carry the firewood to throw onto her husband to burn him further. Ibn Kathir: 4/569.\nExplain the importance of choosing a righteous wife in light of this verse.\nwords\nوَلاَ أَنَا عَابِدٌ مَا عَبَدتُّمI will not worship, in the future, the null deities that you worship\nلَكُم دِينُكُمYou have your religion, and your shirk\nوَلِيَ دِينِI will devoutly adhere to the Oneness of Allah, seeking nothing else\nوَالفَتحُConquest of Makkah, which occurred in the year 8th Hijri\nتَبَّتRuined, perished, and that is a prayer against Abu Lahab\nجِيدِهَاHer neck"],[604,"§Al-Ikhlas, Al-Falaq, An-Nas\ndeeds\nRecite these Suras three times in the morning and evening.\nRecite these Suras once after every prescribed prayer.\nRecite these Suras as a \"Ruqyah\" (supplication for healing) for yourself.\nguid\nIt is imperative to believe in the Oneness of Allah and be sincere to Him.\nSeeking refuge with Allah from the evil eye and witchcraft is important.\nIt is crucial to seek refuge with Allah from the devil's whispers because they are the source of all evils.\nrefl\nقُلۡ هُوَ ٱللَّهُ أَحَدٌ ١\nThere is a debate among scholars about the meaning of the hadith of the Prophet (ﷺ) in which he said: \"(Say, He is Allah, the One) is equivalent to a third of the Quran.\" Some said: Reciting this surah is equivalent in reward to reciting a third of the Quran. Others said: It is equivalent to a third of the Quran because it contains one of the three knowledge areas of the Quran: Tawhīd (Monotheism), laws and narrations. Since this Surah comprises Tawhīd, then it is equivalent to a third of the Quran in this sense, which is more prevalent. Ibn Juzay: 2/624.\nWhat are the three knowledge areas of the Quran? To which one does this surah belong?\nٱللَّهُ ٱلصَّمَدُ ٢\nIbn Al-Anbari said: There is no difference of opinion among the Arabic linguists that Al-Samad is the Master who has no superior and to whom the people turn for the fulfillment of their wishes and needs. AL-Zajjaj said: Al-Samad is he in whom sovereignty has been perfected, and to whom one turns for the fulfillment of one's needs and wishes. Abu Huraira said: He Who is independent of all and all others are dependent upon Him. Al-Alusi: 30/273-274.\nWhat is the meaning of Allah's holy name: Al-Samad?\nوَمِن شَرِّ حَاسِدٍ إِذَا حَسَدَ ٥\nThe word translated here as (envier) also includes the one who puts the evil eye on others, as the evil eye only emanates from an envier who is evil in nature. Al-Saadi 937.\nDoes this Surah include one who puts the evil eye on others? Explain.\nقُلۡ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ ٱلنَّاسِ ١ مَلِكِ ٱلنَّاسِ ٢ إِلَٰهِ ٱلنَّاسِ ٣\nIn Surat Al-Falaq, \"seeking refuge\" comes with one attribute of Allah (the Lord of daybreak) to fend off three evils, but in this Surah, \"seeking refuge\" comes with three attributes of Allah to fend off one evil, which indicates the seriousness of this single evil. Al-Shanqiti: 9/183.\nIn Surat Al-Falaq, \"seeking refuge\" comes with one attribute of Allah against three evils, but here comes with three attributes of Allah against one evil. Why?\nقُلۡ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ ٱلنَّاسِ ١ مَلِكِ ٱلنَّاسِ ٢ إِلَٰهِ ٱلنَّاسِ ٣\nOne may ask: Why are the attributes of Allah stated in this order: Lord, Sovereign, and God? The answer is: These attributes are in ascending order. \"Lord\" can be used for a person who is an owner of a house, etc. \"Sovereign\" is exclusively used for kings, who are in a higher status than people. \"God\" is a higher level than a king, hence, kings never claim to be gods because there is only One God that Has no partner nor parallel, and that's why the stated attributes end with \"God.\" Ibn Juzay: 2/631.\nwhy are the attributes of Allah stated in this order: Lord, Sovereign, and God?\nمِن شَرِّ ٱلۡوَسۡوَاسِ ٱلۡخَنَّاسِ ٤\nThe devil's whispering into a human chest are of many types: Corrupting one's faith and casting doubts on one's beliefs, If the devil fails in this attempt, he incites him to commit sins, when he fails again, he discourages him from performing his religious duties, and when he -again- fails, he tempts him with the desire to be seen by others in order to nullify his good deeds. If the believer survives all of these attempts, the devil tries to make him think highly of himself and his deeds, which can be very harmful to him. Moreover, the devil tries to provoke him with envy, grudges and anger in order to push him to do evil actions. Ibn Juzay: 2/631.\nWhat are the devil's steps of whispering into human chests?\nمِنَ ٱلۡجِنَّةِ وَٱلنَّاسِ ٦\nAllah states that the whisperer can be from among mankind. Alhasan said: They are two devils: The jinn devil whispers into human chests and the human devil comes out in the open. Qatadah said: There are devils among the Jinn and among mankind. Seek refuge with Allah from human devils and jinn devils. Al-Qurtubi: 22/583.\nAre there devils from among Mankind? What is the believer's duty toward them?\nwords\nالصَمَدُThe Self-Sufficient Master, Whom all creatures need\nكُفُوًاEquivalent, Parallel, Comparable\nأَعُوذُI seek refuge\nغَاسِقٍA dark night\nإِذَا وَقَبَWhen the darkness of night settles\nالنَفَّاثَاتِ فِي العُقَدِWomen or evil spirits who practice witchcraft when they blow in knots\nالخَنَّاسِRetreating at the remembrance of Allah's name"]])